CRASH-19: return at once when an output reader function gets a NULL handle

Every SMO_* getter tests the handle with "if (p_data == NULL) errorcode = -1;"
and then returns set_error(p_data->error_handle, errorcode), which
dereferences the NULL handle. Return the error code from the NULL test
instead (-1, or 410 in SMO_getElementName, as before), as SMO_getVersion()
and SMO_getFlowUnits() already do. SMO_getUnits() also read p_data->Npolluts
before its NULL test, and SMO_clearError() had no test at all.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-19_swmm530.patch

